            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "WELY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I freeze the roasted peppers in small amounts wrapped in Saran, then in a Ziploc, and use them all year."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jan"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I use the sweet, multicolored mini-peppers. Wash them and roast without removing seeds or membranes. They are perfect right out of the oven, no need to peel. Depending on your taste you might want to add a touch of salt. They are ready to eat or use in other recipes. (of course do not use or eat the stem.)",
            "datePublished": "2012-05-01T10:41:56.513Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Charliegirl"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent results. Very easy to do. The reviewer who ended up with dried up peppers probably left them too long in the oven. Since the peppers are quartered before being put in the oven, I only needed to cook them for about 20 minutes. The skin got scorched and the peppers were juicy and tender. The roasted peppers were put in a container immersed in garlic and olive oil. They can keep in the refrigerator for up to 2 weeks. So good with crusty bread!",
            "datePublished": "2013-12-16T17:55:04.310Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sassyani2000"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an easy recipe that is also amazingly delicious!\n\nA few changes:\n\n1. This recipe is not restricted to just red bell peppers, I like to use red, yellow and orange-it makes a very colorful combination.\n\n2. I don't cut them before I cook. Once they're roasted, the seeds come right out.\n\n3. I actually love the taste of the skin, so I don't cook these quite as long, and instead just cut them up with the skins on.\n\nA wonderful recipe, and always a huge success at parties!",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-22T05:12:13.443Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Community"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an easy recipe that is also amazingly delicious!\n\nA few changes:\n\n1. This recipe is not restricted to just red bell peppers, I like to use red, yellow and orange-it makes a very colorful combination.\n\n2. I don't cut them before I cook. Once they're roasted, the seeds come right out.\n\n3. I actually love the taste of the skin, so I don't cook these quite as long, and instead just cut them up with the skins on.\n\nA wonderful recipe, and always a huge success at parties!",
            "datePublished": "2011-12-22T05:12:13.443Z"
          },
